        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: complete pinned repair validation",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- complete the remaining acceptance criteria from https://github.com/openclaw/clawsweeper/issues/492 after https://github.com/openclaw/clawsweeper/pull/494 landed\n- prove four moving-main review attempts keep one captured base and final synchronization receives one exact validation/review\n- classify a validation failure as external only after the same command reproduces the same normalized diagnostic on an isolated pinned-base checkout\n- fail closed when dependency/toolchain inputs changed or the pinned ref is unavailable, so baseline reproduction cannot reuse contaminated dependencies\n- preserve repair scope for changed or ambiguous diagnostics, document the final-sync contract, and add the missing changelog entry with reporter credit\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe first landed repair pinned the main execution paths and renewed publication credentials, but its moving-base coverage was source-level and its validation path did not deterministically distinguish a genuine pinned-base failure from a repair-induced failure reported in an unchanged file.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `pnpm run lint:repair`\n- `pnpm run test:repair` — 711 passed\n- `pnpm run test:coverage:changed` — 100% lines/functions, 88.61% branches\n- `pnpm run format:check`\n- focused built repair/CLI suite — 59 passed\n- source-blind behavior contract — all 6 clauses passed, including invalid-base rejection\n- autoreview — clean; no accepted/actionable findings\n\nHosted proof on the first exact head:\n\n- Linux/Windows CI: https://github.com/openclaw/clawsweeper/actions/runs/29146638078\n- CodeQL: https://github.com/openclaw/clawsweeper/actions/runs/29146638063\n- ClawSweeper review: https://github.com/openclaw/clawsweeper/actions/runs/29146639484\n\nThat live review caught dependency contamination in the first pinned-base checkout implementation. The follow-up isolates the boundary by refusing external-base classification whenever manifests, lockfiles, workspace files, or toolchain selectors differ; regression coverage exercises unstaged, staged, and committed dependency changes plus an unavailable pinned ref.\n\n`pnpm run check` reaches the existing macOS harness failures unchanged from `origin/main`: two Bash 3.2 lowercase-expansion tests and one missing-Corepack fixture. The repair suite and changed-surface gates are green; hosted Linux CI remains the full-suite authority.\n\nCloses https://github.com/openclaw/clawsweeper/issues/492\n",
